						Urban collectives—Soul Fire Farm (NY), D-Town Farm (Detroit), Black Dirt Farm Collective (MD)—revive land with ancestral techniques, restoring degraded soils, forging food sovereignty, and rewriting urban law in practice. These actions serve as testbeds for the BLEUE protocol, translating soil health into financial autonomy, environmental data into distributed wealth.
						
